.TH BUFFER_CHUNKED_ENCODE 3
.SH NAME
buffer_chunked_encode \- encode a buffer as the chunked transfer encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int buffer_chunked_encode(buffer* " b ", buffer* " other ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR buffer_chunked_encode ()
initializes
.I b
as a buffer that writes what is put into it to
.I other
as chunks: every flush of
.I b
(also the one that happens when its 1024 byte buffer is full) becomes one chunk. Closing
.I b
with
.BR buffer_close (3)
flushes it, writes the last chunk and flushes
.IR other ;
.I other
is left open.
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 if the memory is short.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
buffer enc;

buffer_chunked_encode(&enc, &conn_out);
buffer_puts(&enc, "hello ");
buffer_flush(&enc);             /* chunk "6\er\enhello \er\en" */
buffer_puts(&enc, "world");
buffer_close(&enc);             /* "5\er\enworld\er\en0\er\en\er\en" */
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_chunked(3), http_chunk(3)
